 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "Nineteen forty-two.",
   "s": 0.0,
   "e": 1.306
  },
  {
   "text": "Germany rolls out the Tiger,",
   "s": 1.717,
   "e": 3.363
  },
  {
   "text": "the most powerful tank in the world.",
   "s": 3.619,
   "e": 5.54
  },
  {
   "text": "It can hit an enemy tank from a mile away.",
   "s": 5.949,
   "e": 8.235
  },
  {
   "text": "Shells bounce off it like peas.",
   "s": 8.645,
   "e": 10.428
  },
  {
   "text": "For every kill,",
   "s": 10.951,
   "e": 11.743
  },
  {
   "text": "the crew paints a ring on the barrel.",
   "s": 11.907,
   "e": 13.55
  },
  {
   "text": "On the other side,",
   "s": 14.184,
   "e": 15.004
  },
  {
   "text": "the Soviets are building their T-34s in a tractor factory.",
   "s": 15.138,
   "e": 18.414
  },
  {
   "text": "Crude welds.",
   "s": 18.792,
   "e": 19.695
  },
  {
   "text": "Rough edges.",
   "s": 19.92,
   "e": 20.628
  },
  {
   "text": "The Germans laugh.",
   "s": 21.159,
   "e": 22.218
  },
  {
   "text": "You're fighting us with tractors?",
   "s": 22.562,
   "e": 24.088
  },
  {
   "text": "You see,",
   "s": 24.747,
   "e": 25.105
  },
  {
   "text": "the Tiger was built like a pocket watch.",
   "s": 25.276,
   "e": 27.255
  },
  {
   "text": "Every gear hand-fitted.",
   "s": 27.631,
   "e": 29.033
  },
  {
   "text": "Every part made for that one tank.",
   "s": 29.448,
   "e": 31.559
  },
  {
   "text": "Then autumn comes.",
   "s": 32.154,
   "e": 33.382
  },
  {
   "text": "Mud.",
   "s": 33.786,
   "e": 34.162
  },
  {
   "text": "Then winter.",
   "s": 34.636,
   "e": 35.255
  },
  {
   "text": "One frozen morning, a Tiger's gearbox cracks.",
   "s": 35.813,
   "e": 38.721
  },
  {
   "text": "A new one has to come all the way from Germany.",
   "s": 39.108,
   "e": 41.222
  },
  {
   "text": "That takes weeks.",
   "s": 41.629,
   "e": 42.468
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile,",
   "s": 43.049,
   "e": 43.582
  },
  {
   "text": "a T-34 loses a wheel.",
   "s": 43.727,
   "e": 45.436
  },
  {
   "text": "The driver walks to a wreck,",
   "s": 45.944,
   "e": 47.266
  },
  {
   "text": "pulls one off,",
   "s": 47.531,
   "e": 48.206
  },
  {
   "text": "and hammers it on.",
   "s": 48.347,
   "e": 49.181
  },
  {
   "text": "It fits.",
   "s": 49.665,
   "e": 50.178
  },
  {
   "text": "Because every T-34 is the same underneath.",
   "s": 50.624,
   "e": 53.317
  },
  {
   "text": "So every broken tank is a parts shop.",
   "s": 53.752,
   "e": 55.847
  },
  {
   "text": "Germany built about thirteen hundred Tigers.",
   "s": 56.562,
   "e": 59.073
  },
  {
   "text": "The Soviets built over fifty thousand T-34s.",
   "s": 59.458,
   "e": 62.727
  },
  {
   "text": "So the Tiger kept winning fights,",
   "s": 63.152,
   "e": 64.879
  },
  {
   "text": "and kept losing the war.",
   "s": 65.02,
   "e": 66.205
  },
  {
   "text": "And that Tiger with the cracked gearbox?",
   "s": 66.814,
   "e": 68.528
  },
  {
   "text": "Its crew is still waiting in the snow,",
   "s": 68.995,
   "e": 70.91
  },
  {
   "text": "watching the tractors roll past.",
   "s": 71.176,
   "e": 72.695
  }
 ]
